| # | Incident | Commit Introduced | Fix Commit | Root Cause |
|---|----------|------------------|-----------|-----------|
| #3 | Task 4: evidence claimed "eval set loaded" + "staleness PASS" from a stub that printed hardcoded strings | d102b90 | 7b7e924 | run.ts was TODOs; evidence described behavior the code did not have |
| #4 | Task 3/4: 10/13 prices in price-snapshot.json fabricated from memory (1000× inflation from wrong unit normalization masked by bare-catch silent fallback) | 0cbd566 | 7b7e924 + bc99d0b | Pricing API queried by model ID (not display name) → zero matches → silent snapshot fallback → snapshot filled from memory |
| #5 | Task 5: micro-routing labels fabricated (33/46 wrong; single-label assumption on fan-out routing; 22 events matched zero rules but got plausible queues) | 20d65f0 | 302d341 | Labels came from intuition, not from evaluating the committed R-1..R-7 patterns |
| #6 | FINDING-H: scorer.ts hardcoded 0.7 threshold; scoreMultiLabel existed but was never called in production path; reports claimed behavior the call graph did not have | 39d20eb | 67fc48f | Unit tests passed on isolated functions while production path bypassed them |
| #7 | FINDING-I: 4 schema sets (100 tasks) nested expectedSchema inside expectedOutput (object, not string); "valid JSON conforming to EvalTask schema" claim was false | f0a5c3f (pre-existing) | f0a5c3f | Type violation undetected because no shape-validation test existed |
| #8 | Task 9: Register figures for 3 entries came from memory/cross-seat copy, not from cited reports | ae946ee | e7e5751 | Figures written without executing a trace grep against the cited files |

**Standing lessons applied:**
- Every numeric figure in a traceability artifact must come from an executed command's output (grep/cat the cited file)
- The eval-set-shape.test.ts prevents incidents #5/#7 class from recurring
- The scorer call-graph spy test prevents incident #6 class from recurring
- The pricing fixture regression tests prevent incident #4 class from recurring

